      "side": 0,
      "message": "That would be a slightly more self-contained form of patchset 1. I think it would probably work in practice, but it also seems like it would produce undefined behavior as implemented. `get_state_pe` assumes that the current state is one of the enum-indexed states and does pointer math on the states to recover the index in the form of an enum. When this race condition is triggered, the current PE state is `NULL`. So the return value probably would not be a valid enum value and probably would trigger underflow. (Enums with no negative values may have unsigned storage classes.)",
